Third-party notices for rulec
=============================

rulec's built-in namespace of first-level divisions (src/prelude.rs, DESIGN.md §15.182)
holds names taken from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository:

  Unicode CLDR 48.2 (release-48-2, 2026-03-17), https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr
    common/subdivisions/en.xml       English names of the subdivisions
    common/subdivisions/{zh,ko,hi,fr,es,it,de,pt}.xml
                                     the names in each country's language
    common/subdivisions/{ca,eu,gl,cy}.xml
                                     co-official names (Catalonia, the Balearic Islands, the
                                     Valencian Community, the Basque Country, Navarre,
                                     Galicia, Wales)
    common/subdivisions/ja.xml       held against the prefectures rulec already had
    common/supplemental/subdivisions.xml
                                     which subdivisions belong to which country
    common/main/en.xml               the names of the five US territories, which the
                                     subdivisions file leaves to the territory names

The names were written into src/prelude.rs (with spaces and hyphens as `_`, and the English
names folded to ASCII) and held against ISO 3166-2 and each government's list; DESIGN.md
§15.182 lists where the table departs from CLDR and why. rulec reads nothing at run time.

